Filed by langertha-llm-advisor, 2026-09-01. Provider docs read 2026-09-01, no live calls.

## The code

`Role::Tools::format_tool_results` (lib/Langertha/Role/Tools.pm:365-378) rebuilds the assistant
echo for the `openai` dialect from exactly three keys:

    my $choice = $data->{choices}[0];
    return (
      { role       => 'assistant',
        content    => $choice->{message}{content},
        tool_calls => $choice->{message}{tool_calls} },
      map { Langertha::ToolResult->new(...)->to('openai') } @$results,
    );

Everything else on the assistant message is discarded -- including `reasoning_content`,
`reasoning` and `reasoning_details`. The `ollama` branch (:308-317) does the same and discards
`message.thinking`.

By contrast the `anthropic` (:288-291), `gemini` (:302-305) and `responses` (:327-339) branches
echo the RAW provider structure, so thinking blocks / thought parts / reasoning items survive
there. The `openai` branch is the odd one out, and it is the branch ~20 engines use.

## Why that is a hard error, not a nicety

DeepSeek, https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/thinking_mode/ (read 2026-09-01): when `tools` is
present, **all prior turns' `reasoning_content` must be sent back or the API returns HTTP 400.**
Without `tools` it is ignored. `Engine::DeepSeek::default_model` is `deepseek-v4-flash`, a
thinking model, and thinking mode explicitly DOES support tools.

So: `Langertha::Engine::DeepSeek` + `chat_with_tools_f` (or `Langertha::Raider`, or
`Langertha::Chat`) fails with a 400 on the SECOND iteration of any tool loop. Every one of the
three loops routes through the same `format_tool_results`, so all three are affected.

Same obligation, softer failure modes, on four more providers:

- **Moonshot / Kimi** (platform.kimi.ai/docs/guide/use-thinking-models): `kimi-k3` has always-on
  preserved thinking and "within one tool-call loop all `reasoning_content` must be sent back".
  `Engine::Moonshot::default_model` is `kimi-k3`.
- **OpenRouter** (openrouter.ai/docs/guides/best-practices/reasoning-tokens): `reasoning_details`
  must be round-tripped "unmodified" and the sequence "must match exactly". Encrypted blocks
  (`reasoning.encrypted.data`) and signatures (`reasoning.text.signature`) live there.
- **Mistral** (docs.mistral.ai/capabilities/reasoning/): the assistant message must be replayed
  including its `ThinkChunk`; stripping it "significantly degrades output quality".
- **xAI** (docs.x.ai prompt-caching): "you must include `reasoning_content` from previous
  responses" or the prompt cache misses.

## Minimal fix direction

Echo the raw assistant message and add the tool_calls, rather than rebuilding three fields:

    my $msg = $data->{choices}[0]{message};
    return ( { %$msg, role => 'assistant' }, ...results... );

That is a strict superset of today's behaviour for every provider (the extra keys are exactly the
ones the providers asked us to send back) and it makes the `openai` branch behave like the other
four. Risks to check before doing it:

- `Langertha::Chat` / `Raider` push these elements into `session_history`, which is rendered for
  the `raider_session_history` self-tool -- a fatter assistant element must still render (see the
  comment at Raider.pm:898-906, which already documents that element shapes differ per dialect).
- Some OpenAI-compatible servers reject unknown keys on an inbound assistant message. Unknown
  today; worth one probe per major provider, or a per-engine allowlist of echo keys if a strict
  server turns up.
- Mistral's `content` is an ARRAY during thinking; `{ %$msg }` passes it through unchanged, which
  is what Mistral wants. (Note the separate hazard that `Langertha::Response.content` is
  `isa => 'Str'` and would die on that array -- see k129.)

This is a correctness bug on a documented hard-error path, not a design question. Higher severity
than k129 (which is about the STREAM parsers); k129's advisor note cross-references this ticket.
